# pi-coder settings for THIS checkout only.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored, so it is never cloned) to pin pi-coder's own environment for a
# development checkout while a copy installed by pi keeps the defaults. Precedence: a variable
# already set in the environment wins over a value in this file.
#
# Only pi-coder's own prefixes are applied: PI_CODER_*, PI_SANDBOX_*, PI_MEMORY_*, SANDBOX_*,
# COMPACTION_*, DECISION_MODEL_*, AGENT_CONFIG_*. `HOME`, `PATH`, and pi's own `PI_*` settings are
# ignored on purpose — pi has already resolved its config by the time an extension loads.
#
# Run pi with PI_CODER_ENV_FILE=0 to ignore this file for one launch, or set it to a path to use a
# different file. `#` starts a comment; quote a value that needs leading or trailing spaces.

# Keep this checkout's runtime state (delegated transcripts, worktrees, decision log, compaction
# trace, run database, profiles) in its own `.state/`, so switching branches keeps the same state.
# A relative value resolves against this checkout, whichever project directory pi was started in.
# An installed copy has no `.env` and uses `<agent-dir>/pi-coder`, which pi's `git clean -fdx`
# cannot wipe.
PI_CODER_STATE_DIR=.state

# Other knobs a development run may want. Unlike the state root, path values are used as given,
# so spell them absolutely.
# PI_CODER_AGENT_TRACE=1
# SANDBOX_DECISION_LOG=0
# COMPACTION_TRACE=0
# PI_SANDBOX_BACKEND=bwrap